From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 02:42:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia: don't run past the buffer on NULL elements in an ACPI
 package

nv_acpi_extract_object() returns success for a NULL package element without
setting its size, so nv_acpi_extract_package() counts the previous element's
size again. With the buffer nearly full, buffer_size underflows and the next
element is copied past the end of the buffer. The returned size can also exceed
the buffer, which callers trust.

Clamp the gap and the returned size to what's left in the buffer. Packages that
fit keep the layout they have now, including the gaps, because the fields are
read by position.

nv_acpi_evaluate_dsm_method() also returned an uninitialized size for an object
of an unsupported type. Start it from 0.

Tested the parsing in userspace, old against new: the old code writes past an
8-byte buffer and the new one doesn't. Not hit on real firmware.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
index 0303ada0..b50f226e 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/nv-acpi.c
@@ -668,6 +668,11 @@ static NV_STATUS nv_acpi_extract_package(
     *data_size = 0;
     for (i = 0; i < acpi_object->package.count; i++)
     {
+        //
+        // A NULL element doesn't set element_size, so it leaves a gap the size
+        // of the previous element. That gap may not fit in what's left.
+        //
+        element_size = NV_MIN(element_size, buffer_size);
         buffer = ((char *)buffer + element_size);
         buffer_size -= element_size;
 
@@ -676,7 +681,7 @@ static NV_STATUS nv_acpi_extract_package(
         if (status != NV_OK)
             break;
 
-        *data_size += element_size;
+        *data_size += NV_MIN(element_size, buffer_size);
     }
 
     return status;
@@ -885,7 +890,7 @@ static NV_STATUS nv_acpi_evaluate_dsm_method(
     union acpi_object *dsm = NULL;
     struct acpi_buffer output = { ACPI_ALLOCATE_BUFFER, NULL };
     union acpi_object dsm_params[4];
-    NvU32 data_size;
+    NvU32 data_size = 0;
 
     if (!NV_MAY_SLEEP())
     {
